<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />

<p>The accuracy of a Riemann sum approximation increases as...</p>

<answer name="ans1a">
  <choice credit="1">the number of intervals increases</choice>
  <choice>long as the right-hand Riemann sum is taken, rather than the left-hand Riemann sum. </choice>
  <choice>long as the left-hand Riemann sum is taken, rather than the righ-hand Riemann sum.</choice>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>The following sum means...</p>
                        
  <me>I_r = \sum_{i=1}^{5} g(t_i)\Delta t</me>
<answer name="ans2a">
  <choice>the right hand Riemann sum is <m>I_r = g(t_1)^1 + g(t_2)^2 +....+g(t_5)^5</m></choice>
  <choice>the right hand Riemann sum is <m>I_r = g(t)\Delta t_1 + g(t)\Delta t_2 +....+g(t)\Delta t_5</m></choice>
  <choice credit="1">the right hand Riemann sum is <m>I_r = g(t_1)\Delta t + g(t_2)\Delta t +....+g(t_5)\Delta t</m></choice>
</answer> 
</exercise>

</problem>
</section>